Removed Replacement <code>nested.abs</code>, <code>exp</code>, <code>exp2</code>, <code>expm1</code>, <code>log</code>, <code>log2</code>, <code>log10</code>, <code>log1p</code>, <code>acos</code>, <code>acosh</code>, <code>asin</code>, <code>asinh</code>, <code>atan</code>, <code>atanh</code>, <code>cos</code>, <code>cosh</code>, <code>sin</code>, <code>sinh</code>, <code>tan</code>, <code>tanh</code> <code>apply_to_tensors(data, torch.xxx)</code> from <code>batchtensor.utils.structure</code> <code>nested.clamp(data, min, max)</code> <code>apply_to_tensors(data, partial(torch.clamp, min=..., max=...))</code> <code>nested.as_tensor(data)</code> <code>coola.recursive.recursive_apply(data, torch.as_tensor)</code> <code>nested.combine(items, fn)</code> <code>batchtensor.utils.structure.combine_tensors(items, fn)</code> <code>nested.split(data, fn)</code> <code>batchtensor.utils.structure.split_tensors(data, fn)</code> <code>batchtensor.nested.types.NestedTensor</code> <code>batchtensor.nested.NestedTensor</code> (public, excludes <code>str</code> and <code>bytes</code>). The module is now <code>batchtensor.utils.types</code>; <code>batchtensor.nested.types</code> is removed <pre><code>&gt;&gt;&gt; import torch
&gt;&gt;&gt; from functools import partial
&gt;&gt;&gt; from batchtensor.utils.structure import apply_to_tensors
&gt;&gt;&gt; batch = {"x": torch.tensor([[-1.0, 2.0]])}
&gt;&gt;&gt; apply_to_tensors(batch, torch.exp)
{'x': tensor([[0.3679, 7.3891]])}
&gt;&gt;&gt; apply_to_tensors(batch, partial(torch.clamp, min=0.0))
{'x': tensor([[0., 2.]])}
</code></pre>
